<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe Newspapers boosts half-yr shr.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe Newspapers boosts half-yr shr.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended June 30.</p>
<p>	   (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		    121.0 vs  44.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		     30.0 vs   7.5</p>
<p>    Trading profit		22.2 vs  10.5</p>
<p>    Interest received	    3.9 vs   0.5 paid</p>
<p>    After-interest profit     26.1 vs  10.0</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		26.6 vs  10.1</p>
<p>    Taxation			9.1  vs   3.8</p>
<p>    After-tax profit	    17.4 vs   6.3</p>
<p>    Turnover		     185.0 vs 152.2</p>
<p>Div payable Oct 11</p>
<p>on register Sept 13.</p>
<p>Full name: Zimbabwe Newspapers Group</p>
<p>NOTE - The group forecast share earnings for the year ending December 31 at over 240 cents, providing there were no major increases in input costs during the next six months. It said it would incur major capital expenditure -- estimated at Z$50 million -- within the next 12 months on pre-press processes, printing machinery, desktop publishing and computers. It said the money would come from the group's own resources and long-term market finance.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
